course: dictionary
lesson: 12565
title: Dietary: to do with food
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Dietary comes from diet, which is what a person usually eats and drinks. So if something is dietary, it is about food. Look at the words around it: they often name food or a rule about food.
explain: «Our school asks about dietary requirements before every party.» The clue is party and asks. The school wants to know which foods each child can or cannot eat. Swap in the meaning: "asks about food rules before every party" still makes sense.
explain: «Oats and beans give you dietary fibre, which helps your tummy stay healthy.» Fibre is a part of some foods, and helps your tummy work well. Here dietary tells you the fibre is part of what we eat.
fact: Dietary means to do with food, or with a diet.
fact: «Dietary needs» are the foods a person can or cannot eat.
fact: «Dietary requirements» can come from health, religion or beliefs, such as vegetarian or halal.
fact: «Dietary fibre» is found in foods like oats, beans and apples, and helps digestion.
fact: Schools ask about dietary requirements so that everyone is safe, especially children with allergies.
exercise: «The school asks about dietary requirements before the party.» What does dietary mean here? | To do with the school bus | To do with homework | *To do with food rules, such as what a person can eat | Things that please the eyes
exercise: «Dietary fibre helps your tummy stay healthy.» Which food could contain dietary fibre? | Fizzy drink | *Oats | Crisps | Sweets
exercise: Mia says, «I cannot have nuts because of my dietary needs.» What does dietary needs mean? | Ways to stay up late | A kind of bike | *The foods a person can or cannot eat | Games played at break time
test: «Our cook checked every child's dietary requirements before making the lunch.» What are dietary requirements? | Sports kit needed for games | Pictures of food on the wall | *The food rules a person must follow | Shops in the town
test: Which word means to do with food and what we eat? | *Dietary | Library | Diary | Dictionary
exam: Which sentence uses dietary correctly? | She painted a dietary bright blue sky | *The school checked the children's dietary needs before the trip | The dog ran dietary across the park | The bus stopped dietary at the station
